    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Farm Operations Workflow Automation\n\n**Purpose:** Automate farm and pond record collection, data validation, storage, and alert notifications using n8n.\n\n**How it works:**\n1. **Receive Data:** Accepts pond records through a webhook.\n2. **Validate Records:** JavaScript checks required fields, numeric values, and valid measurement ranges.\n3. **Route Records:** Invalid submissions receive an error response, while valid records proceed to storage.\n4. **Store Data:** Saves valid pond measurements and feeding records to Google Sheets.\n5. **Monitor Conditions:** Checks measurements against configured thresholds and sends email alerts for abnormal conditions.\n\nAlert Logic:\n\nDissolved oxygen < 5 mg/L → Send a low-oxygen alert.\n\nTemperature > 35°C → Send a high-temperature alert.\n\nAll measurements within configured alert thresholds → No alert email.\n\nMissing fields or invalid measurements → Reject the submission and return an error response.\n\n**Tech Stack:** n8n · Webhooks · JavaScript · REST APIs · Google Sheets · Email Notifications\n",
        "height": 448,
        "width": 688
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
